66cb1a36-106c-498a-aa99-25639c31e42f	EMAIL	OUTLOOK	\N	johnhilton@wiper.pl	\N	johnhilton@wiper.pl	2026-04-01 16:20:47	Hi Majid. I have attached a drawing of our standard showerlay. Its for 800mm x 800mm but generally the only difference with the larger trays is the size and drain length. Generally the rule is that the drain length is 300mm less than the side of the showerlay on which it lies. So a 1200mm showerlay width with a 900mm drain, that's 150mm each side of the drain to the edge (D1) and 150mm from the edge of the showerlay to the side of the drain (C1). With a 20mm thick showerlay, the linear drain body will pertrude from the underside of the showerlay. This would need some thought on a wooden floor but not on a screeded concrete floor With 30mm and 40mm the linear drain body is more or less level with the underside of the showerlay. All are produced from XPS foam covered both sides in a cementous coating and reinforced net. The drain is factory built into the foam and is waterproofed into place. All showerlays have slopes from each corner to the corner of the linear drain. As with all cement coated showerlays, they must be waterproofed before tiling. I hope this helps. Thanks. John. Best regards John Hilton Export Sales Director e-mail: johnhilton@wiper.pl tel.: +48 32 738 50 00 | mob.: +48 515 286 062 WIPER Sp. z o.o., ul. Kolejowa 2, 43-190 Mikołów, Polska NIP 635-16-05-660, KRS 0000212232 www.wiper.pl poczta@wiper.pl	Tech Drawing	\N	\N	\N	NEW_ENQUIRY_CANDIDATE	0.00	{}	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	f	f	\N	\N	\N	\N	d9255dcc-1985-4ce0-abb1-9003c29e7e5b	\N	\N	2026-04-16 09:15:45.904	2026-04-16 09:15:45.908
