tique and luxury hotel interiors Hypnos UK Premium Hotel Bedding Supplying five-star and luxury hotel projects Villeroy and Boch Germany Tiles / Sanitaryware / Tableware Active across hospitality and residential segments Tarkett France Commercial Flooring Supplied into hospitality and commercial segments Vicaima Portugal Interior Doors / Joinery Specified in hotel and residential construction Flos Italy Designer Lighting Specified in five-star and lifestyle hotel projects Morocco Hospitality Market: Key Numbers Indicator Figure Active hotel pipeline 85+ projects under development New rooms in development 150,000+ FF&amp;E and OS&amp;E procurement mandate $3B+ through 2030 Tourism target 26 million visitors by 2030 FIFA World Cup 2030 co-hosts Morocco, Spain and Portugal - largest shared hospitality cycle in history Europe: share of Morocco's import market Dominant across most hospitality categories - but under pressure China: Morocco import market rank Top 3 and growing - aggressively targeting hospitality supply Morocco: local manufacturing capacity Limited - high import dependency across all major categories Luxury and upper-upscale pipeline share 40%+ of active projects - strongest segment for European brands Procurement decisions being made Now - for projects opening 2026, 2027, and 2028 Enquire Now The FIFA World Cup 2030 deadline is not 2030. The hotels opening for the World Cup are being specified and procured right now. Developers are meeting with procurement teams. Interior designers are finalising material selections. FF&amp;E decisions for projects opening in 2026 and 2027 are being confirmed in the current quarter. European brands that are visible and commercially active in front of these buyers will win specification. Those that are not present will find their categories filled by alternatives - and re-entering a supply chain after specification is locked is significantly harder than being inside it from the start. The 6th Hospitality Innovation Summit 