9b5169d1-0b3c-43a3-8b52-28e9efac94ac	EMAIL	OUTLOOK	\N	Harry.Johns@criterioncapital.co.uk	\N	Harry.Johns@criterioncapital.co.uk	2026-04-01 18:27:37	Hi Harry, I have attached a drawing of our standard showerlay. Its for 800mm x 800mm but generally the only difference with the larger trays is the size and drain length. Generally the rule is that the drain length is 300mm less than the side of the showerlay on which it lies. So a 1200mm showerlay width with a 900mm drain, that's 150mm each side of the drain to the edge (D1) and 150mm from the edge of the showerlay to the side of the drain (C1). With a 20mm thick showerlay, the linear drain body will pertrude from the underside of the showerlay. This would need some thought on a wooden floor but not on a screeded concrete floor With 30mm and 40mm the linear drain body is more or less level with the underside of the showerlay. All are produced from XPS foam covered both sides in a cementous coating and reinforced net. The drain is factory built into the foam and is waterproofed into place. All showerlays have slopes from each corner to the corner of the linear drain. As with all cement coated showerlays, they must be waterproofed before tiling. I hope this helps. Thanks. John. Kind regards, Majid Al Jassas Managing Director | Cromwell Plumbing Ltd E: majid.aljassas@cromwellplumbing.co.uk T: +44 203 621 0938 M: +44 777 609 9987 W: www.cromwellplumbing.co.uk A: Ground Floor 423 Harrow Road London W10 4RE This email and any files transmitted with it are confidential and intended solely for the use of the individual or entity to whom they are addressed. If you have received this email in error please notify us immediately and then permanently delete it. Although we make every effort to keep our network free from viruses, you should check this email and any attachments to it for viruses as we cannot accept any liability for viruses inadvertently transmitted by us. Registered in England and Wales. Cromwell Plumbing Limited Regi