ommunications through its internal and external networks in accordance with applicable law. No Advice: Unless expressly stated otherwise and confirmed in a separate formal advice letter, nothing in this email constitutes legal, financial, tax or investment advice. No duty of care is assumed. You should seek appropriate professional advice before acting on any information contained herein. Authorisation: No email instruction shall authorise expenditure or create contractual obligations unless confirmed by a duly executed purchase order or written contract signed by an authorised signatory of Criterion Capital Limited. From: Omar Orders &lt; Omar.Orders@criterioncapital.co.uk &gt; Sent: 02 April 2026 10:57 To: Majid Al Jassas &lt; majid.aljassas@cromwellplumbing.co.uk &gt;; Harry Johns &lt; Harry.Johns@criterioncapital.co.uk &gt; Cc: Jas Kalsi &lt; Jas.Kalsi@criterioncapital.co.uk &gt; Subject: Re: ref. orders awaiting review &amp; approval Have we ordered this? From: Majid Al Jassas &lt; majid.aljassas@cromwellplumbing.co.uk &gt; Sent: 01 April 2026 18:27 To: Harry Johns &lt; Harry.Johns@criterioncapital.co.uk &gt;; Omar Orders &lt; Omar.Orders@criterioncapital.co.uk &gt; Cc: Jas Kalsi &lt; Jas.Kalsi@criterioncapital.co.uk &gt; Subject: Re: ref. orders awaiting review &amp; approval [CAUTION: THIS IS AN EXTERNAL EMAIL. PLEASE DOUBLE CHECK THE EMAIL ADDRESS. Do not click links or attachments that are unexpected or from unknown senders.] Hi Harry, I have attached a drawing of our standard showerlay. Its for 800mm x 800mm but generally the only difference with the larger trays is the size and drain length. Generally the rule is that the drain length is 300mm less than the side of the showerlay on which it lies. So a 1200mm showerlay width with a 900mm drain, that's 150mm each side of the drain to the edge (D1) and 150mm from the edge of the showerlay to the side of the drain (C1). With a 20mm thick showerlay, the linear drain body will pertrude from the underside of the showerlay. This would need some thought on a wooden floor but not on a screeded concrete floor With 30mm and 40mm the linear drain body is more or less level with the underside of the showerlay. All are produced from XPS foam covered both sides in a cementous coating and reinforced net. The drain is factory built into the foam and is waterproofed into place. All showerlays have slopes from each corner to the corner of the linear drain. As with all cement coated showerlays, they must be waterproofed before tiling. I hope this helps. Thanks. John. Kind regards, Majid Al Jassas Managing Director | Cromwell Plumbing Ltd E: majid.aljassas@cromwellplumbing.co.uk T: +44 203 621 0938 M: +44 777 609 9987 W: www.cromwellplumbing.co.uk A: Ground Floor 423 Harrow Road London W10 4RE This email and any files transmitted with it are confidential and intended solely for the use of the individual or entity to whom they are addressed. If you have received this email in error please notify us immediately and then permanently delete it. Although we make every effort to keep our network free from viruses, you should check this email and any attachments to it for viruses as we cannot accept any liability for viruses inadvertently transmitted by us. Registered in England and Wales. Cromwell Plumbing Limited Registration No. 10611686. Registered Address: Cromwell Plumbing, Ground Floor 423 Harrow Road London W10 4RE From: Harry Johns &lt; Harry.Johns@criterioncapital.co.uk &gt; Date: Tuesday, 31 March 2026 at 16:42 To: Majid Al Jassas &lt; majid.aljassas@cromwellplumbing.co.uk &gt;, Omar Orders &lt; Omar.Orders@criterioncapital.co.uk &gt; Cc: Jas Kalsi &lt; Jas.Kalsi@criterioncapital.co.uk &gt; Subject: RE: ref. orders awaiting review &amp; approval Apologies, you are correct. Can you share the datasheets for the Wiper product Harry Johns Criterion Capital Criterion Capital C/O Zedwell Hotel, Great Windmill Street, London Trocadero, London, W1D 7DH Telephone – Switchboard 0207 432 2444 w