f87c7450-12a3-4021-af76-e6c430bca224	a6ee1419-a8cf-414c-89c4-29e4d9660d8a	Subject: LUTON MOSQUE - DOUCHE\nFrom: Asif Usmani <Asif@reach-cm.co.uk>\nDate: 2026-04-09T12:38:12Z\n\nSalam Majid, I hope you are well. Can you provide a quote for the below, documents attached, for our site in Luton. Option 1 Supply and install 8 nos of CAT 5 WARS approved mini break tank for WC above the flushing cistern Brand : Arrow Valves Model : BTHW-1 Option 2 Supply and install 1 nos of CAT 5 WARS approved booster set with 3 nos of 12kw electrical instantaneous water heater with all necessary pipes runs Booster Set Brand: Dutypoint 90L Model : VQ-03-007 single phase 1.3 l/s 45m H Water Heater Brand: Stiebel Eltron Model : DCE-S 10/12 Plus Attached all relevant catalog ue and draft schematic for your reference . I look forward to hearing from you. Kind regards ​ ​ ​ ​ Asif Usmani Procurement Manager T: +442070466359 WINNER: London Construction Awards 2025, Commercial Project of the Year, The Hobson ​FINALIST: London Construction Awards 2025, Commercial Project of the Year, The Wellington 50 Havelock Terrace, London SW8 4AL | Main: +44 (0)20 7046 6311 ​Company registered in England &amp; Wales. Registered address: 14th Floor, 33 Cavendish Square, London W1G 0PW. Registered no: 14654487 ​ Disclaimer: The information contained in this communication is confidential. It is intended solely for use by the addressee. If you are not the addressee, any disclosure, copying, distribution or taking action in relation to this information is strictly prohibited and may be unlawful. The Company undertakes all reasonable efforts to ensure this communication has been scanned for viruses, etc, however email transmission cannot be guaranteed as secure.\n\n--- bthwdatasheet-5.pdf ---\n\n\nQ:\\Arrow Valves\\Products\\BT Break Tanks\\BTHW Ablution Plant\\bthwdatasheet.docx  21-Nov-25 \nArrow Valves Ltd \nTel: 01442  823123      Fax: 01442  823234   \nwww.arrowvalves.co.uk \n \nArrow Valves Ltd reserve the right to change specifications,  \ndesign and materials at any time without notice. \nAll unit-less dimensions in mm. \n© Copyright Arrow Valves Ltd 2009-2025 \n \n \nModel BTHW-1 \ndelivers safe hot \nwater with  \nFluid Category 5 \nbackflow protection \nDescription \nThe Ablution Plant unit delivers hot water at the required safe \ntemperature with the highest backflow protection.  The primary \napplication is bidets or ablution hoses adjacent to a WC or \nbidet.  The unit can also be used for many other applications \nrequiring hot water with Fluid Category 5 protection. \n \nToiletry applications are strictly Fluid Category 5, requiring a \npoint of use air gap from the mains water or building supply \npipe.  There is a duty of care to provide warm water at a safe \ntemperature with suitable legionella controls in place. \n \nThe Ablution Plant is packaged in a cabinet - consisting of – \n \n• Wall Bracket \n• Solenoid filled Break tank with type AB air gap complying \nwith BSEN13077: 2003 \n• Booster Pump \n• Water Heater with thermostat and safety relief valve \n• Thermostatic Mixing Valve (TMV3, DO8) \n• Controls, fittings and sound proofing \n \nThere is a growing need to provide international toiletry \nfacilities.  This Ablution Plant helps with Muslim Qada al-\nHaajah requirements and forms part of the performance of \nWudhu (Ablution for Prayer). The Ablution Plant is normally \nbehind a removable panel in a washroom and delivers warm \nwater to a trigger operated hose (supplied separately) adjacent \nto a toilet, bidet or wash area.  This enables the users to \nhygienically clean themselves possibly without toilet paper.   \n \nThe unit automatically switches on when a pressure drop is \ndetected – e.g. when the user operates the trigger valve on the \nhose - optional extra.  The pump has a “soft start” feature, \nwhich avoids water and electrical surges.  The pump and \nheater are protected via a low level float switch in the cistern. \n \nTo enable a standard 13 A supply to be used - thus avoiding \nhigh current demands - the unit incorporates a 5 litre heater, \nwhich is factory set to 62\nO \nC (Legionella bacteria die within 32 \nmins in water @ 60\no \nC).   \n \nThe internal TMV blends the hot water down to 38\nO \nC \n(adjustable), which is maintained for a period – see Hot Water \nCapacity.  An additional cold water outlet with Fluid Category 5 \nprotection is optional (BTHW-OP1). \n \nThe unit is quiet by virtue of a high quality brass pump fitted \nwith anti-vibration mounts, stainless braided internal hoses and \nthick fire proof sound insulation. \n \nThere are several optional upgrades – see page 2 \n \nWater Regulations \nBidets and any hoses used for toiletry purposes are classified \nas Fluid Category 5—the highest contamination risk—requiring \na suitable air gap. \n \nTo prevent internal cross-contamination, WCs and bidets must \nhave point-of-use Category 5 protection. In hotels, this typically \nmeans one unit per bathroom, as commonly required by water \ncompanies. \n \nFor legionella control, terminal fittings should reach final \ntemperature within 30 seconds, typically achievable with ≤5 m \nof 15 mm copper pipe (G18.4). \n \n \nApplications \nPublic buildings such as hotels, education departments, \nhospitals, healthcare and government buildings now frequently \ncater for multi-cultural use and are being suitably equipped. \n• Ablution hose adjacent to a WC \n• Bidets - ascending spray or with a flexible hose \n• Medical & mortuary tables \n• Veterinary & animal washing \n• Laboratories \n• Butchery \n \nAblution Plant - Model BTHW \nSafe Hot Water with Fluid Category 5 Protection – Datasheet – Page 1 of 2 \n \n \n \n \nSpecification \nPressure Supply \nbar 0.8 (min.) / 10 (max.) \nInlet Temperature \n°C 1 to 25 max. \nOutlet Temperature \n°C \n30 – 50 ± 2 (38 factory set) \n(Tamperproof adjuster in cabinet) \nSafety Relief Valve \nbar 6 (pressure relief) \nWater Reg. Approval \nStatus \n  2211706 \nElectrical Specification \nVoltage / Frequency \nV / Hz 230 (1 Phase) / 50 \nPower Consumption \nkW 2  (heater) + 0.4 = 2.4  \nFull Load Current \nA 10.2 (inc. heater) \nHeater Controls \n  \nThermostat, safety temperature cut-\nout (manual reset) \nLow Level Protection \n  Pump and heater (auto reset) \nMaterials \nCabinet \n  Steel – powder coated RAL7032 \nPump Wetted Parts \n  Brass  \nHeater Wetted Parts \n  Stainless Steel \nPipes / Fittings \n  Copper / Brass / Stainless \nCabinet Insulation \n  Sound absorbing fire retardant \nHoses \n  WRAS approved stainless braid \n \nConnection Pipes \nA stainless steel braided hose with Y strainer and servicing \nvalve is supplied - as required by the Regulations (G16.4).  \nThe outlet and pressure relief are 15 mm Tectite. \n \nCodes and Descriptions \n \n \nSize Code Description \n15 mm BTHW-1 Ablution Unit-1 Hot FC5 TMV 230 V \n \n \n \n  \n \n \n\nQ:\\Arrow Valves\\Products\\BT Break Tanks\\BTHW Ablution Plant\\bthwdatasheet.docx  21-Nov-25 \nArrow Valves Ltd \nTel: 01442  823123      Fax: 01442  823234   \nwww.arrowvalves.co.uk \n \nArrow Valves Ltd reserve the right to change specifications,  \ndesign and materials at any time without notice. \nAll unit-less dimensions in mm. \n© Copyright Arrow Valves Ltd 2009-2025 \n \n \n \nAblution Plant - Model BTHW \nSafe Hot Water with Fluid Category 5 Protection – Datasheet – Page 2 of 2 \nHot Water Capacity \nThe standard unit (5 litre heater) at a flow rate of 0.07 Lt/s, can \nsupply water at 38\nO\n C for 2 minutes then a reducing \ntemperature for a further minute.   \n \n \nPump Performance \nThe standard unit is limited to 0.07 Lt/s but user can change to \n0.1 Lt/s and more pressure to the nozzle. \n \n \n \nInstallation Considerations – see O&M Manual \nThe unit should be mounted at a serviceable height.  There \nmust be sufficient clearance under the base of the cabinet to \nconnect the overflow. \n \nThe servicing valve with flow limiter and flexible hose must be \nused. \n \nThe overflow/warning pipe should discharge in a safe and \nconspicuous manner.  The safety relief valve also discharges \nvia the overflow connection at the base of the cabinet. \n \nElectrical - supply via a 2 pole isolator and RCD or RCBO.  \n \nOptions \n• Ablution hose and trigger Chrome. \n• Cold water outlet (FC5 protection) in addition to hot \n• Automatic Tank Purge – legionella control \n• Drip Tray – catches any leaks from a faulty unit \n• BMS fault monitor (BTBMS3) – volt free with changeover.  \nActivates fault lamp and BMS relay if tank water level is \ntoo high or low, or if there is a low pressure fault. \n• Remote Thermostatic Mixing Valve (if >5 m pipe run) \n \nCode Description \nCSHT-2 Ablution Hose & Trigger Chrome \nBTHW-OP1 Ablution FC5 Cold Water Outlet Option \nBTHW-OP2 Automatic Tank Purge System /24h \nBTHW-1RTMV BTHW-1 with Remote TMV \nBTBMS3B BTMD/BTHW Alarm BMS - Volt Free \nBTDT4 Drip Tray for Midi range Stainless \n \n \nDimensions \nHeater recovery time is approx \n5 sec for every 1 sec use  \n@ 0.1 Lt/s. \nE.g. typical 18 seconds use \nrequires 1.5 minutes  \nto fully recover \n \n--- se_383_SE_A3_Inst Water Heaters_COUNTER MAT_18.2.26pdf.pdf ---\n\n\nProduct Comparison | Instantaneous Water Heaters\nSTIEBEL ELTRON UK Ltd | Unit 12 Stadium Court | Bromborough | CH62 3RP | Telephone 0151 346 2300 | sales@stiebel-eltron.co.uk | www.stiebel-eltron.co.uk\n1) Sink 10/12KW only  where endless supply is more important than flow | 2) IP 25 Guaranteed only if appropriate \ncable grommets and O-rings are fitted on the twin pipe connections (see installation manual)\nProduct CategoryComfort Instantaneous Water HeatersCompact Instantaneous Water HeatersMini Instantaneous Water Heaters\nPremiumPlusPremiumPlusPremium\nProduct TypeDHEDHB-E LCDDCE-X PremiumDCE-S PlusDEM\n204284 (18/21/24 kW)\n204285 (27 kW)\n203866 (18/21/24 kW)\n203865 (27 kW)\n238158 (7.2/9.6 kW)\n238159 (12/14.3 kW)\n238153 (7.2/9.6 kW)\n238154 (12/14.3