eans  all  products,  materials,  equipment,  plant,  machinery,  components,  and  items \n(including packaging) to be supplied by the Supplier under the Purchase Order.\n"Services" means any work, labour, installation, commissioning, testing, consulting, design, or other \nservices to be provided by the Supplier under the Purchase Order.\n"Delivery  Address"  means  the  location  specified  in  the  Purchase  Order  for  delivery  of  goods  or \nperformance of services.\n"Delivery  Date"  means  the  date  or  dates  specified  in  the  Purchase  Order  by  which  delivery  or \nperformance must be completed, time being of the essence.\n"Variation Order" or "VO" means a written instruction issued by the Company authorising a change \nto the scope, specification, quantity, or price of the goods and/or services.\n"Specification"  means  the  description,  drawing,  design,  or  technical  requirements  for  the  goods \nand/or services as set out in or referred to in the Purchase Order.\n"Price" means the sum stated in the Purchase Order as payable for the goods and/or services.\n"Insolvency  Event"  means  where  the  Supplier  enters  into  administration,  liquidation,  bankruptcy, \nreceivership, enters into a company voluntary arrangement or individual voluntary arrangement, has \na receiver or administrative receiver appointed, ceases or threatens to cease trading, or is unable to \npay its debts as they fall due.\n"Authorised  Signatories"  means  Harry  Johns,  the  appointed  Person,  members  of  the  Company's \nLegal Department, or such other persons as notified in writing by the Company from time to time.\n"Business  Day"  means  a  day  (other  than  Saturday  or  Sunday)  on  which  banks  are  open  for  general \nbusiness in London.\n"Writing"  includes  email  to  the  designated  Company  contact  addresses  specified  in  the  Purchase \nOrder.\n1.2  Interpretation.  References  to  clauses  are  to  clauses  of  these  terms  and  conditions.  Headings  are  for \nconvenience only and do not affect interpretation. Words importing the singular include the plural and vice \nversa.\n\n2. PRECEDENCE AND ENTIRE AGREEMENT\n2.1 Exclusive application. These terms and conditions are the only terms applicable to the Purchase Order \nand   the   supply   of   goods   and/or   services.   The   Supplier's   own   terms   and   conditions   (howsoever \ncommunicated) are expressly excluded and shall not apply, even if referenced in the Supplier's quotation, \nacknowledgement, delivery note, invoice, or other documentation.\n2.2  Battle  of  the  forms.  If  the  Supplier  seeks  to  impose  or  incorporate  its  own  terms  and  conditions,  the \nCompany's terms and conditions shall prevail in all circumstances. The Supplier's commencement of work \nor  delivery  of  goods  constitutes  unequivocal  acceptance  of  the  Company's  terms  and  conditions  to  the \nexclusion of all others.\n2.3  Entire  agreement.  The  Purchase  Order  (including  these  terms  and  conditions)  constitutes  the  entire \nagreement  between  the  parties  and  supersedes  all  prior  negotiations,  representations,  quotations,  or \nagreements whether written or oral relating to the subject matter.\n2.4 Order of precedence. In the event of any conflict or inconsistency, the following order of precedence \nshall  apply:  (a)  any  written  Variation  Order  signed  by  Authorised  Signatories;  (b)  these  terms  and \nconditions;  (c)  the  Purchase  Order  face  page  (quantities,  prices,  delivery  dates);  (d)  any  Specification  or \ntechnical  requirements  annexed  to  the  Purchase  Order;  (e)  the  Supplier's  quotation  (to  the  extent \nexpressly incorporated by reference only).\n2.5  Amendments.  No  amendment,  modification,  or  variation  to  the  Purchase  Order  or  these  terms  and \nconditions shall be valid unless made in writing and signed by Authorised Signatories of the Company.\n3. PRICING, PAYMENT TERMS, AND FINANCIAL CONTROLS\n3.1 Fixed price. The Price stated in the Purchase Order is fixed, firm, and non-variable for the duration of \nthe  contract.  All  prices  are  inclusive  of  all  costs  whatsoever  including  but  not  limited  to:  (a)  labour \n(including   overtime,   shift   premiums,   and   unsocial   hours   working);   (b)   materials,   components,   and \nconsumables;  (c)  plant,  tools,  equipment  hire,  and  scaffolding;  (d)  packaging,  crating,  palletisation,  and \nprotective  wrapping;  (e)  loading,  unloading,  delivery,  carriage,  and  freight;  (f)  insurance  and  risk  during \ntransit;  (g)  fuel  surcharges  and  environmental  levies;  (h)  administration  fees,  handling  charges,  and \nprocessing fees; (i) testing, commissioning, and certification; (j) all licences, permits, and statutory consents \nrequired; (k) waste disposal, site clearance, and making good.\n3.2  No  additional  charges.  No  additional  charges,  uplifts,  variations,  or  supplementary  costs  will  be \naccepted  or  paid  by  the  Company  unless:  (a)  a  written  request  for  variation  has  been  submitted  by  the \nSupplier  and  approved  in  advance;  (b)  a  Variation  Order  has  been  issued  and  signed  by  Authorised \nSignatories;  and  (c)  a  corresponding  revised  Purchase  Order  has  been  issued  confirming  the  amended \nPrice.\n3.3 All-inclusive obligation. The Supplier warrants that it has: (a) fully inspected and assessed the Delivery \nAddress, site conditions, access arrangements, and working environment; (b) made all necessary enquiries \nto ascertain the nature and extent of the goods and/or services required; (c) accounted for all known and \nreasonably   foreseeable   variables,   conditions,   risks,   and   requirements;   (d)   satisfied   itself   as   to   the \ncorrectness  and  sufficiency  of  the  Price.  Failure  to  do  so  does  not  constitute  grounds  for  additional \npayment or extension of time.\n3.4  Price  verification.  The  Price  stated  in  the  Purchase  Order  must  correspond  exactly  with:  (a)  the \nSupplier's quotation (if applicable); (b) any agreed price list or framework agreement; and (c) the Supplier's \ninvoice. Any price discrepancy between the Purchase Order and invoice will result in automatic rejection of \nthe invoice and suspension of payment until rectified at no cost to the Company.\n3.5 Payment terms. Subject to full compliance with these terms and conditions, payment shall be made 30 \ndays  from  the  date  of  receipt  by  the  Company  of:  (a)  a  correctly  submitted  and  compliant  invoice  (see \nclause  6);  (b)  all  required  supporting  documentation  and  evidence;  (c)  proof  of  delivery/completion \n\ndocumentation;  and  (d)  submission  via  the  Company's  designated  procurement  management  system  or \nenterprise resource planning system as notified in writing.\n3.6 Retention. The Company reserves the right to retain a percentage of the Price as follows: (a) standard \nretention  of  5%  of  the  Price  for  Purchase  Orders  valued  at  £10,000  or  more;  (b)  high-value  retention  of \n10% of the Price for Purchase Orders valued at £50,000 or more; (c) retained sums shall be released upon \nthe  later  of:  (i)  expiry  of  the  applicable  defects  liability  period;  or  (ii)  satisfactory  completion  of  all \nrectification  works;  (d)  the  Company  may  deduct  from  retention  any  costs,  expenses,  damages,  or  losses \nincurred due to the Supplier's default, defects, or breach.\n3.7 Set-off and deduction. The Company reserves the right to set off against any sums due to the Supplier \nany amounts owed by the Supplier to the Company under this or any other Purchase Order, including: (a) \ncosts of rectifying defective or non-conforming goods/services; (b) liquidated or unliquidated damages; (c) \nadministration  costs  for  non-compliant  invoicing;  (d)  costs  incurred  due  to  late  deli