he cable cla mp is  used to secure  \nthe cable into posit ion.\nWARNING: \nFAILURE TO COMPLY WITH THESE\nINSTRUCTIONS COULD RESULT IN \nFAILURE OF   THE   TERMINAL BLOCK\nSection 6Fitting \nThe Swivel Arm \nInto Position\nIMPORTANT: Fitting the swivel arm must\nprecedefitt ing the front   cover\n1. Push the swivel arm into the outlet and \ntighten b y turn ing counter clo ckwise until \nswive  l  arm is  tight .\n4\n\nSection 7Fitting \ntheCover into\nPosition\nIt is necessar  y to engagethecontrol knob \non   the correct position   on   the valve spi  ndl  e \nbefore the front   cover is located.\n1. Be  fore  re pla cing the fro nt cover  check that the \nvalve spin dle and temperature  contro l  knob \nare  set to fully anti clo ckwise or full  flow.\n2. Secure  the fro nt cover wit h the two scre ws.\nImportant   inf  ormation\nEnsure  the ro tary temperature  control  is  \npositioned fully anti clo ckwise and that the valve \nis fully open.  \nSection 8\nCommissioning \nProcedure\n1. Switch o n the mains ele ctric  al  supply at the \nisolatin g swit ch.\n2. Ensure  the w ater  supply is  fully on at    the \nmain s and the isolating service valve (if   fitted)\nis fully open.\n3. Place hand in  fro nt of the sensor  lens \napproximately   50-60mm away, the unit will  \nstar   t.\n4. Check that    the w ater  flows freely fro m    the \nhandwash wit hin a few seconds                                                     \n5. Check that    the unit switches off   automatically \nafter  appro ximately   30 seconds\n6. Now switch o ff   the p ower  supply at    th\ne local \nisolator  and then re move the fro nt cover.\n7. Re  move the RE  D LOCK MOULDING by sli ding \nit upwards and away fro m    the pressure  \nswit ch.\n8. Check for  leaks\n9. Re  fit the fro nt cover.\n10.Switch the power  on at local isolator\n11.Place hand in  fro nt of sensor  to restart unit \nand adjust tempera ture contro l  knob to a \ndesired temperature . All ow a few moments \nfor  the tempera ture  to stabili ze.\n12.Turn  contro l  knob anti clo ckwise to check \nwater g ets cooler\nSection 9Operating \nthe Handwash\n1. The main s electric  ity and water  supply should \nnormallybe left on.                                                                    \n                                                                                                        \n2. To operate the handwash, simply pass    your \nhand in front o f the centra l sensor  lens. The \nunit has an infra-re d beam whic h when \nre flected by your  hand swit ches the unit on. \nThe unit can be switched off by the same \nactio n. The unit w ill  shut down after  30 \nseconds.\n3.   Water  is  heated in stantaneously   as it flows \nover  the heating ele ments in  the heat \nexchanger.                                                                  \n4. The flow/tempera ture  is adjusted via   the \ncontro l kno  b, the higher  t\nhe flow the lower \nthe temperature  and the lower the flow the \nhigher  the temperat ure .                                                        \n         \nWait a few moment  s for the \ntemperature of the water to stabilize. \n                                                                   \n4.   If the in coming water  pressure  fall s below a \nset li mit, the pressure  switch will  opera te and \nswit ch off   the power  to the heatin g element\n5\n\nbe le ft on.                                                                                                                                                                               \n                                                                                        \n5.   The unit incorporates a pressure  re li ef devic e \nto safeguard  again st abnormal p ressure  \nconditions and pro vides a safeguard  should \nan excessive b uil dup of pressure  occur wit hin  \nthe unit.\nDEMONSTRATE OPERATION TO USERS, \nAND LEAVE THIS BOOK WITH THEM FOR \nFUTURE REFERENCE.\nWARNING:  